1gsb|n|A piece of cloth, or other suitable material, sewed or otherwise fixed upon a garment to repair or strengthen it, esp. upon an old garment to cover a hole. ; A small piece of anything used to repair a breach; as, a patch on a kettle, a roof, etc. ; A small piece of black silk stuck on the face, or neck, to hide a defect, or to heighten beauty. ; A piece of greased cloth or leather used as wrapping for a rifle ball, to make it fit the bore. ; Fig.: Anything regarded as a patch; a small piece of ground; a tract; a plot; as, scattered patches of trees or growing corn. ; A block on the muzzle of a gun, to do away with the effect of dispart, in sighting. ; A paltry fellow; a rogue; a ninny; a fool.	a:27t7,99,3;1bwk,87,3;27t9,83,8;1nls,73,5;y85,61,4;1wjt,50,3;1on5,48,7;4x4,44,2;1al8,44,3;we0,43,2;v4k,41,1;1vdo,41,2;tug,39,5;zf4,36,1;1owy,36,3~f6m,18,18;16io,8,13;cs2,34,9;27t9,83,8;19rc,16,8;1on5,48,7;1m36,3,7;1dry,3,6;1wie,0,6;17zj,3,6;1r7d,26,5;1nls,73,5;c0q,11,5;45o,2,5;216v,9,5	v:v4k,57,3;27t9,53,1;1v37,31,1;25i3,23,2;433,19,8;1m5j,19,5;1jw,19,1;1v4t,9,2;1pff,5,7;1v0y,3,1;42t,2,3~433,19,8;1pff,5,7;1m5j,19,5;42t,2,3;v4k,57,3;25i3,23,2;1v4t,9,2;27t9,53,1;1v37,31,1;1v0y,3,1;1jw,19,1	V:1gsf,43,5;czi,38,2;190g,37,4;1hyr,33,1;9b8,19,4;s9t,18,3;1p91,18,6;1ytv,15,3;42t,15,7;e99,13,4;1m5j,12,3;1pzk,10,2;5bs,10,5;10mb,7,4;1z7i,5,5~42t,15,7;1mfe,4,6;1p91,18,6;5bs,10,5;1z7i,5,5;dzs,3,5;1gsf,43,5;9b8,19,4;10mb,7,4;j9o,2,4;e99,13,4;190g,37,4;1m5j,12,3;s9t,18,3;1ytv,15,3	n:4a8,76,4;zf4,46,2;1wjt,44,2;y85,41,1;4x4,34,1;u4z,33,5;1v37,31,1;1t56,26,48;24ku,26,6;4bp,23,3;268s,19,3;1fcs,17,3;18ui,17,3;22gj,17,10;nsn,14,4~1t56,26,48;22gj,17,10;f6m,7,8;1ulm,10,6;24ku,26,6;u4z,33,5;4a8,76,4;e6z,11,4;1gol,1,4;qqk,11,4;nsn,14,4;4bp,23,3;1fcs,17,3;1gsb,8,3;268s,19,3	N:1j2x,63,2;1tbp,62,2;bfk,49,2;14id,47,26;246x,44,2;czf,44,11;3f5,40,8;6mb,39,6;czi,38,2;140t,27,2;p9w,25,4;v4j,23,2;rw9,20,1;fop,20,2;qmn,19,6~14id,47,26;czf,44,11;3f5,40,8;6mb,39,6;qmn,19,6;qvj,5,5;p9w,25,4;20ry,11,4;1qau,12