1gvl|n|One who protects, supports, or countenances; a defender. ; A master who had freed his slave, but still retained some paternal rights over him. ; A man of distinction under whose protection another person placed himself. ; An advocate or pleader. ; One who encourages or helps a person, a cause, or a work; a furtherer; a promoter; as, a patron of art. ; One who has gift and disposition of a benefice. ; A guardian saint. -- called also patron saint. ; See Padrone, 2.	N:1rno,138,3~1rno,138,3
